      "ref": "[D502]",
      "area": "contact",
      "claim": "A parent reports that strangers can message or voice chat with your child, and it is on by default but can be turned off.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "Roblox communication settings allow you to control who can interact with you, for example, by only allowing interactions with friends or not allowing any interactions at all. You can also restrict your account, which turns off chat and public commenting and limits an account to certain filtered experiences on Roblox."
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D502]",
      "area": "money",
      "claim": "The app pushes in-app purchases and loot boxes, and it may have pay-to-win features.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "You can buy Robux or premium subscriptions and choose how to pay from our available payment methods. When you pay, you (or your parent or guardian if you’re under 13) will have to give billing information, including Personal Information such as: Our payment processors (for example, PayPal) manage the transactions, which are subject to their terms and conditions and privacy policies."
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D502]",
      "area": "data",
      "claim": "Roblox collects persistent identifiers like IP address and device IDs, and it may share data with third parties for ads or service providers.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "Roblox collects persistent identifiers and the information we ask you for when you sign up for the following internal operations: Roblox implements technical, contractual, and other measures to ensure that persistent identifiers are not used for purposes other than those listed above. Roblox relies on service providers to support the internal operations described above. In some cases, these entities may process persistent identifiers from users."
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D502]",
      "area": "age_gating",
      "claim": "A parent reports that the age gate works in practice, restricting under‑13 users from certain features.",
      "stance": "mitigation",
      "quote": "When children sign up for Roblox, we also collect certain types of personal information called persistent identifiers for internal operations and to provide you and other users with Services. Persistent identifiers are data like IP Address and unique device identifiers that are required for you to be able to connect your device to Roblox. Persistent identifiers can be used to recognize you, your device, or your household device. Roblox collects persistent identifiers and the information we ask you for when you sign up for the following internal operations: Roblox implements technical, contractual, and other measures to ensure that persistent identifiers are not used for purposes other than those listed above."
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D502]",
      "area": "content",
      "claim": "A parent reports that children may see unfiltered chat and public comments that are not fully filtered.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "When users publish anything in our public and comment areas (for example, chat, forums, group walls, personal posts), we filter it and remove: To provide the filtering above, we use human and automated checking to the best of our ability based on available technology – but like all filtering technology, these systems aren’t 100% effective."
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D502]",
      "area": "developer_record",
      "claim": "A parent reports that Roblox has faced regulatory scrutiny and fines related to children's privacy.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "We comply with the Children’s Online Privacy Protection Act (“COPPA”). COPPA affords parents the right to: To exercise these rights, Roblox may require you to take action or provide additional information so we can verify your request, such as linking your account to your child’s account."
